# Copy these lines into the repository's .gitignore.
#
# The first three are vise's own per-checkout state: the journal, the run lock,
# and the probe scratch. `vise init` appends them for you.
.vise/journal.jsonl
.vise/run.lock
.vise/tmp/

# The build cache the probe wrapper writes. This one is load-bearing, not
# housekeeping: vise compares the whole work tree around every judged run, and
# a file Git neither tracks nor ignores is a harness error. An ignored path is
# the one place a probe is allowed to write, and that is exactly what a build
# cache is. Without this line every probe here fails on its first run with
# "wrote files git neither tracks nor ignores".
.gocache/
